============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-Pi space along which the
  pore fraction is preserved: simultaneously rescaling the
  dimensionless groups along g keeps the LPBF physics invariant.

  Generator 1:
    Pi1 x exp(-0.568*eps), Pi2 x exp(-0.163*eps), Pi3 x exp(+0.726*eps), Pi4 x exp(+0.093*eps), Pi5 x exp(-0.240*eps), Pi6 x exp(+0.205*eps), Pr x exp(+0.117*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi3 while decrease Pi1, decrease Pi2, increase Pi4, decrease Pi5, increase Pi6, increase Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 2:
    Pi1 x exp(+0.153*eps), Pi2 x exp(+0.236*eps), Pi4 x exp(+0.953*eps), Pe_vap x exp(-0.067*eps), Pr x exp(+0.082*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi4 while increase Pi1, increase Pi2, decrease Pe_vap, increase Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 3:
    Pi1 x exp(-0.550*eps), Pi2 x exp(+0.095*eps), Pi3 x exp(-0.305*eps), Pi4 x exp(+0.061*eps), Pi5 x exp(+0.677*eps), Pi6 x exp(+0.252*eps), Pr x exp(+0.263*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi5 while decrease Pi1, increase Pi2, decrease Pi3, increase Pi4, increase Pi6, increase Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 4:
    Pi1 x exp(+0.447*eps), Pi3 x exp(+0.232*eps), Pi4 x exp(-0.061*eps), Pi5 x exp(+0.226*eps), Pi6 x exp(+0.817*eps), Pr x exp(-0.154*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi6 while increase Pi1, increase Pi3, decrease Pi4, increase Pi5, decrease Pr
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

